      "role": "user",
      "content": "Climbing Stairs\n\nYou are climbing a staircase with n steps. Each time you can climb 1 or 2 steps. In how many distinct ways can you reach the top?\n\nExample: n = 3 -> 3 (1+1+1, 1+2, 2+1).\nConstraints: 1 <= n <= 45.",
      "id": "m-0",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-09T08:09:07.070Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Complexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.\n\nKey invariant: the data structure state after processing prefix i fully determines the answer for i+1.",
